WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.456
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:14.706
Unit twenty-nine: Natural Disasters. In this unit, you will describe disasters and what was happening.

4
00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:16.787
emergency kit.

5
00:00:17.487 --> 00:00:21.437
emergency kit means a bag of food, water and medicine for emergencies.

6
00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:24.445
Every family should have an emergency kit.

7
00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:27.856
Your turn. Say: emergency kit.

8
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:31.986
emergency kit.

9
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:33.996
rescue team.

10
00:00:34.696 --> 00:00:37.996
rescue team means a group of people who save others in danger.

11
00:00:38.296 --> 00:00:40.528
The rescue team reached the village by boat.

12
00:00:41.228 --> 00:00:43.450
Your turn. Say: rescue team.

13
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.291
rescue team.

14
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:49.482
warning system.

15
00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:53.900
warning system means a system that tells people a disaster is coming.

16
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.650
A new warning system sends text messages before floods.

17
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.852
Your turn. Say: warning system.

18
00:01:03.552 --> 00:01:04.773
warning system.

19
00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:06.726
damage.

20
00:01:07.426 --> 00:01:09.670
damage means harm done to something.

21
00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.561
The storm caused serious damage to the roofs.

22
00:01:13.261 --> 00:01:15.647
Your turn. Say: damage.

23
00:01:18.347 --> 00:01:19.267
damage.

24
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.205
survivor.

25
00:01:21.905 --> 00:01:25.413
survivor means a person who continues to live after a disaster.

26
00:01:25.713 --> 00:01:28.189
The survivors were taken to a safe shelter.

27
00:01:28.889 --> 00:01:31.170
Your turn. Say: survivor.

28
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:34.836
survivor.

29
00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:36.781
aftermath.

30
00:01:37.481 --> 00:01:40.085
aftermath means the period after a disaster.

31
00:01:40.385 --> 00:01:43.116
In the aftermath of the flood, neighbours helped each other.

32
00:01:43.816 --> 00:01:46.236
Your turn. Say: aftermath.

33
00:01:48.936 --> 00:01:49.972
aftermath.

34
00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:51.973
relief aid.

35
00:01:52.673 --> 00:01:56.948
relief aid means food, water and help sent to people after a disaster.

36
00:01:57.248 --> 00:01:59.398
Relief aid arrived from many countries.

37
00:02:00.098 --> 00:02:02.786
Your turn. Say: relief aid.

38
00:02:05.486 --> 00:02:06.603
relief aid.

39
00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:08.908
tropical storm.

40
00:02:09.608 --> 00:02:13.779
tropical storm means a strong storm with heavy rain and wind from warm seas.

41
00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:16.519
A tropical storm hit the coast last night.

42
00:02:17.219 --> 00:02:20.057
Your turn. Say: tropical storm.

43
00:02:22.757 --> 00:02:24.049
tropical storm.

44
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.980
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.337
Where were you when the tropical storm hit?

46
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:35.520
I was staying with my grandparents. We were having dinner when the warning system sounded.

47
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:38.236
Was your village damaged?

48
00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.642
Yes. Many houses were damaged, and the bridge was destroyed.

49
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.683
Were people rescued quickly?

50
00:02:47.983 --> 00:02:52.505
Yes. A rescue team arrived, and relief aid was sent the next day.

51
00:02:53.817 --> 00:02:57.755
Grammar focus: Past continuous + past passive.

52
00:02:58.055 --> 00:03:01.401
Use the past continuous for background actions in the past.

53
00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:04.990
Use the past passive to say what happened to people or things.

54
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.193
For example: We were sleeping when the storm hit, and many roads were flooded.

55
00:03:09.493 --> 00:03:14.395
News reports often use the past passive because the event is more important than who did the action.

56
00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:18.129
Now read and listen. When the River Rose.

57
00:03:18.429 --> 00:03:22.564
In October, heavy rain was falling for six days in western Cambodia.

58
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.883
Rivers were rising quickly, and many villages were flooded.

59
00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:31.030
Thousands of people were moved to schools and pagodas.

60
00:03:32.317 --> 00:03:36.778
Rescue teams were sent with boats, and relief aid was delivered by truck.

61
00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:41.581
In the aftermath, families worked together to repair the damage.

62
00:03:42.883 --> 00:03:45.222
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:45.522 --> 00:03:48.834
A bag of food, water and medicine for emergencies is an blank.

64
00:03:49.134 --> 00:03:52.950
A, emergency kit. B, aftermath. C, survivor.

65
00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.333
The answer is A: emergency kit.

66
00:04:00.817 --> 00:04:02.909
We blank TV when the lights went out.

67
00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.677
A, watched. B, were watching. C, are watching.

68
00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.532
The answer is B: were watching.

69
00:04:14.017 --> 00:04:15.645
The bridge blank in the storm.

70
00:04:15.945 --> 00:04:19.981
A, was destroyed. B, destroyed. C, was destroying.

71
00:04:23.983 --> 00:04:26.018
The answer is A: was destroyed.

72
00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:29.981
The period after a disaster is the blank.

73
00:04:30.281 --> 00:04:34.619
A, relief aid. B, warning system. C, aftermath.

74
00:04:38.617 --> 00:04:40.837
The answer is C: aftermath.

75
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.605
According to the text, where were people moved?

76
00:04:44.905 --> 00:04:49.499
A, to hotels. B, to schools and pagodas. C, to the capital.

77
00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:55.843
The answer is B: to schools and pagodas.

78
00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:01.256
Now it's your turn to speak. What should be in a family emergency kit?

79
00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:13.188
It should include water, rice, a torch, batteries, medicine and copies of important documents.

80
00:05:13.488 --> 00:05:15.023
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:16.017 --> 00:05:21.154
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past continuous + past passive.

82
00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:24.768
Today's value is being prepared. Get ready before you go.

83
00:05:25.068 --> 00:05:27.244
See you in Unit thirty. Goodbye!

84
00:05:27.544 --> 00:05:30.103
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

